! repositioning.inp
! -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
! Header format (one line):
!   NPTS  VWINCH  Kp  Ki  Kd  DBpos  DBvel
! where
!   - Kp, Ki: PI gains acting on sway error (positive error shortens the
!     upwind line / pays out the downwind line depending on the sign).
!   - Kd: virtual damping opposing sway velocity (in m/s); larger Kd reduces
!     oscillations but slows the maneuver. Start small (e.g. 10–30% of Kp in
!     equivalent units) and increase until the sway response is acceptably
!     overdamped without stalling.
!   - DBpos: position deadband [m]. Inside this band, proportional action is
!     suppressed and the integral term pauses to prevent windup.
!   - DBvel: velocity deadband [m/s]. When both |error| <= DBpos and
!     |ydot| <= DBvel, winching stops entirely so the controller does not
!     re-energize low-damped modes near the target.
!   - VWINCH: rate limit [m/s] applied to the commanded rest-length change.
! Tuning guidance:
!   1) Pick VWINCH based on desired slew speed of the winch hardware.
!   2) Increase Kp until the floater tracks ramps without steady-state bias.
!   3) Add Ki slowly to eliminate residual bias while keeping the response
!      smooth (beware of oscillations if Ki is too high).
!   4) Add Kd to damp sway/roll coupling; raise it until overshoot disappears
!      but the motion still progresses. If response becomes sluggish, back off
!      Kd or slightly raise Kp.
!   5) Set DBpos and DBvel to the “done” tolerance (e.g. a few meters and a few
!      cm/s) so actuation stops when close and slow.
! -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
6   0.05   0.02   0.001  0.02  1.0  0.05

! t[s]   y_target[m]
0     0
100   0
101  50
300  50
301 -50
500 -50
600   0
